{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524096-homebrew-minor-template-the-faint-a-thought-exercise-for-daywalkers-sort-of","id":1524096,"title":"[Homebrew Minor Template] The Faint - a thought exercise for Daywalkers... sort of","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-15T06:34:28-07:00","id":1524096,"title":"[Homebrew Minor Template] The Faint - a thought exercise for Daywalkers... sort of","content":"Daywalkers are a cool concept, of course. What I have in mind here, however, is closer to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XLZKg8J6QF0\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>: entirely common and normal human by day, but come dusk, turning into something else. This minor template attempts to give an option to play the latter option e.g. as an alternative to Ghouls.<br /> <br /> Now, just giving Kindred the ability to move about during the day even as a simple human would be incredibly boring and jarring fluff-wise, taking away their biggest limitations and weaknesses, while also very overpowered. This is ChroD, after all, so how to play up the Horror?<br /> This was my line of thought for this thought experiment. Meet the Faint: some say the result of a failed attempt at establishing a clan, others point to the Ordo and claim a botched experiment. Others say this could have happened to everyone, an Embrace having gone wrong somehow. Whatever the case, Faint can be seen as twice-cursed rather than once-blessed.<br /> <br /> Yes, they can walk around during daytime, but there is a price to be paid:<br /> For one, sunlight still is incredibly uncomfortable and being in the sun essentially counts as a Level 3 environment (under the effects of Blazing and Extreme Heat whenever out in the open or in direct sunlight, essentially) and the Beast is still triggered. Of course, everything that smells of Vitae or Blood Potency is not available during the day - these are, for all intents and purposes, very sun-averse and sunburn-prone, people with a weird and short fuse, but otherwise normal. They need food, get hungry and sleepy, bleed normally etc etc.<br /> <br /> But when night rolls around, they transform! Literally. Skin pales, eyes change, fangs slightly grow - not enough to draw attention from strangers, but very noticeable to close ones or people being around during the process. The Faint get access to their Vitae, and with it their disciplines and the most basic abilities of Kindred existence. Well, kind of: the transformation is a half-measure. Their body is still, technically, alive, so they take damage as mortals do. And they tire, and breath, and age - staying up 24/7 is NOT an option without Exhausting oneself, and despite getting older much more slowly, they do get older. At least the Blush of Life is considered always on. They need to drink blood in addition to food, but have only limited access to the Kiss (not painful, but not pleasant, either, and the vicim's mind doesn't get as foggy). Whatever stores of Vitae they had are scoured by the rising sun, so they start each night at 0 Vitae, and must acquire something quickly, or contend with the Beast. Ending the night with less than 1 Vitae three days in a row results in 1L damage, as the body cannibalizes it's own blood.<br /> There are no in-Clan Disciplines, of course.<br /> However, their Vitae is exceptionally potent: due to their technically living nature, each point of Faint Vitae yields three points of normal Vitae, and this also applies in regards to causing Vinculum.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is as far as I've gotten.<br /> <br /> As of now, there is little incentive to have these in the game aside from maybe a curiosity, I'm afraid. Any feedback on making these Kindred shooting stars into something coherent and fitting the game would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T08:07:56-07:00","id":1524098,"title":"","content":"I think, as is, your first draft is quite confused. Are these changes to the ghoul template, changes to the kindred template, a replacement for ghouls? They seem to be super blood dolls more than anything else.<br /> <br /> I think if we go back to your core idea we can find several possible paths. The first and probably easiest is a take on the bloodline that mixes two clans, I would go Nosferatu and Gangrel. For disciplines they can have Gangrel disciplines + Nightmare or Nosferatu disciplines + Protean depending on their original clan, they have both clan banes and perhaps their bloodline gift reduced their effective blood potency during the day time with a reduction to 0 or below rendering all their vampiric powers unavailable but removing their weaknesses as well. Or maybe that would be a bloodline specific merit or devotion. There's lot of ways to tinker with it mechanically without having to do too much work.<br /> <br /> Another option I think is making it a merit template. While I love merit templates I don't think this idea has a lot of merit and it would be the most work, creating merits and tying them to vampiric abilities. Or you could reflavor an existing merit template, maybe the military drug one? Still not a fan of this route though.<br /> <br /> The last idea is that maybe it's a take on a hunter conspiracy, members are modified with vampiric viate upon joining and this is the result. I think the idea of a hunter who is basically newly embraced every night and who vomits up any blood he drank at dawn could have a lot of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T11:24:02-07:00","id":1524112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524096-homebrew-minor-template-the-faint-a-thought-exercise-for-daywalkers-sort-of?p=1524098#post1524098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, as is, your first draft is quite confused. Are these changes to the ghoul template, changes to the kindred template, a replacement for ghouls? They seem to be super blood dolls more than anything else.<br /> <br /> I think if we go back to your core idea we can find several possible paths. The first and probably easiest is a take on the bloodline that mixes two clans, I would go Nosferatu and Gangrel. For disciplines they can have Gangrel disciplines + Nightmare or Nosferatu disciplines + Protean depending on their original clan, they have both clan banes and perhaps their bloodline gift reduced their effective blood potency during the day time with a reduction to 0 or below rendering all their vampiric powers unavailable but removing their weaknesses as well. Or maybe that would be a bloodline specific merit or devotion. There's lot of ways to tinker with it mechanically without having to do too much work.<br /> <br /> Another option I think is making it a merit template. While I love merit templates I don't think this idea has a lot of merit and it would be the most work, creating merits and tying them to vampiric abilities. Or you could reflavor an existing merit template, maybe the military drug one? Still not a fan of this route though.<br /> <br /> The last idea is that maybe it's a take on a hunter conspiracy, members are modified with vampiric viate upon joining and this is the result. <b>I think the idea of a hunter who is basically newly embraced every night and who vomits up any blood he drank at dawn could have a lot of potential.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> (emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> It's basically supposed to be a minor template, so more like an alternate Kindred template (not replacement, as it sets out to explore different things).<br /> I think the Bloodline idea would simply end up overpowered, because a Vampire who doesn't have to worry about Sunlight or Daysleep at all just has (most of ) the best of both worlds. I wanted this to be a Blessed with Suck kind of deal (because for some reason, I like those). So yeah, I suppose they are Super Blood dolls. But blood dolls that get you unexpectedly into Vinculum courtesy of surprisingly potent blood... hm... I feel like that could be a thing. Playing up the too-weak nature, maybe throw in the Honey Trap merit, make them appear too delicious and defenseless a meal to pass up for high-potency Kindred, only to go the &quot;Gotcha, sucker&quot; bit because they quite quickly establish power over their would-be-masters. <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> I *love* the bolded idea. A group of modified human 'Kindred' with access to some Kindred abilities, but distinctly different from Ghouls, with their own bag of sucky downsides, but a unique apporach to fight Kindred.<br /> <br /> I shall tinker and return =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T12:28:25-07:00","id":1524113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524096-homebrew-minor-template-the-faint-a-thought-exercise-for-daywalkers-sort-of?p=1524112#post1524112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Bloodline idea would simply end up overpowered, because a Vampire who doesn't have to worry about Sunlight or Daysleep at all just has (most of ) the best of both worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not worrying about the sun at all would be over powered, that's why I only recommended having a slightly higher functioning humanity or slightly lower blood potency. Remember young vampires already don't have much to worry about from the sun. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I *love* the bolded idea. A group of modified human 'Kindred' with access to some Kindred abilities, but distinctly different from Ghouls, with their own bag of sucky downsides, but a unique apporach to fight Kindred.<br /> <br /> I shall tinker and return =D </div> </div> </div>I look forward to seeing what you come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}